I recently started playing NetHack again, after having given up on it
for the same reasons I'm annoyed now. Perhaps someone would like to hear
opinions about the game playability, so here's what I think:

- Wizards are almost unplayable. If the Rings they're provided with at
the beginning are worn all the time (not always necessary, I know), one
runs out of food very soon - which is hard to find on the first levels
(I know, praying helps, but it just runs out so damn quickly)

- The player should get the chance to discover traps by chance, ie. some
kind of automatic searching like the Elves', but without cost. It's
natural that someone just strolling around would sometimes spot a pit
full of spikes. That this doesn't happen is annoying, because it's just
a matter of luck whether your 1-5th level character will drop on poison
spikes which are deadly at the instant. Having to rely on luck at all
should be removed from the game completely - I understand that you don't
*have* to drink eg. from fountains or sinks, but traps are annoying. You
can't search all the time since you'll run out of food quickly, either.

I found the original 'hack' more playable than NetHack in these aspects.

Also, there should be a 'real' manual. You just have to know too much
about the game to be able to play. Normally, you'd imagine that a magician
trained all his life to go on this quest would know what a wand of
cancellation does, but *I* don't, and have no chance of finding out
besides looking at the source code. [If this is in the 'Guide to the
Mazes of Menace', I'm sorry, wrong example. :-)]

